# stub-claude-fixtures.manifest — the reviewed disposition of every test file
# that builds its own `claude` stub. your-org/nexus-code#764.
#
# Columns (TAB-separated):
#   1 path          repo-relative
#   2 step          which resolver step the CONSTRUCTION lands on: local|path
#   3 claude-bin    does the file assign CLAUDE_BIN?
#   4 guard         does it call th_require_stub_claude?
#   5 disposition   pinned | no-resolver | exposed | selftest
#   6 reason        why that disposition — required, and reviewed
#
# Columns 1-4 are FACTS, regenerated by `stub-claude-fixtures.sh`; column 5-6 are
# the human verdict. `test-stub-claude-manifest.sh` fails when 1-4 drift from the
# classifier, so a NEW fixture that stubs `claude` lands here unclassified and red.
#
# THE AXIS. `monitor/_claude-bin.sh` resolves `$CLAUDE_BIN` -> then
# `$NEXUS_ROOT/node_modules/.bin/claude` -> then PATH. The `#746` hazard
# (`locals-env.sh` re-fronting `$NEXUS_LOCALS/bin` via BASH_ENV) can only bite at
# the PATH step. So:
#
#   pinned       construction decides the resolution before PATH is consulted —
#                either CLAUDE_BIN (step 1) or the fixture's own
#                node_modules/.bin/claude under its own NEXUS_ROOT (step 2).
#                Immune by construction, whether or not it reaches the resolver.
#   no-resolver  step 3, but MEASURED never to reach `_claude-bin.sh` at all.
#   exposed      step 3 AND reaches the resolver. MUST call th_require_stub_claude.
#   selftest     drives the guard's own pass and refuse arms on purpose.
#
# HOW REACHABILITY WAS ESTABLISHED. Not by reading. `_claude-bin.sh` was
# instrumented with an entry trace and a fail-closed interlock, and every member
# was executed under a decoy nexus whose `claude` is a stub (so the hazardous
# re-fronting stayed active but no billed binary was reachable). The REACH counts
# below are measured; `reach=0` means the resolver was never sourced. Two arms
# proved the instrument fires: `test-spawn-worker-resume.sh` traced 34 reaches,
# and `test-respawn-loop-integration.sh` resolved to the DECOY locals copy rather
# than its own stub — the hazard reproducing, and its guard refusing.
#
# VERDICT ON THE ISSUE'S CANDIDATE LIST OF 22: none of the 22 is `exposed`.
# 16 are `pinned`, 5 are `no-resolver`, and one — `test-version-restart-self.sh` —
# creates no `claude` stub at all (the grep matched `install-claude-local.sh`), so
# it is absent below. The two genuinely exposed sites are the one `#759` already
# fixed and `test-integration/_harness.sh`, which the list does not contain.
#
monitor/watcher/test-bootstrap-claude-install.sh	local	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Passes CLAUDE_BIN explicitly per run and drives the resolver's fail-loud arm; reach=0 (bootstrap stubbed).
monitor/watcher/test-cc-auto-update.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	Creates $root/claude for the cc-auto-update version probe, selected via CC_AUTO_CLAUDE_BIN, not _claude-bin.sh; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-cc-restart-watchdog-loop.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $root/node_modules/.bin/claude under its own root; step 2 beats PATH; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-cc-restart-watchdog-verify.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $root/node_modules/.bin/claude under its own root; step 2 beats PATH; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-claude-loop.sh	path	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Passes CLAUDE_BIN=$STUB_BIN/claude on every invocation; measured reach=10, all resolving to that stub via step 1.
monitor/watcher/test-entry.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	Stub exists so a pane process is NAMED claude for entry.sh's liveness walk; nothing spawns it through the resolver; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-gh-identity.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Empty node_modules/.bin/claude only so a link-nexus-tools precondition holds; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-install-claude-local.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	The npm symlink IS the artifact under test; step 2 path by definition; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-install-shell-hook.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	Fake locals/bin/claude proves the rc hook puts `claude` on PATH by name; asserts PATH resolution directly, never _claude-bin.sh; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-instance-heartbeat.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at node_modules/.bin/claude as a spawn precondition; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-instance-lock.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at node_modules/.bin/claude as a spawn precondition; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-integration/_harness.sh	path	no-claude-bin	guarded	exposed	Shared harness for 5 scenarios: fronts $HARNESS_BIN on PATH, exports NEXUS_ROOT=$HARNESS_DIR, pins NOTHING. In ambient env it resolved to the operator's real locals/bin/claude. Guarded here, once, for every caller.
monitor/watcher/test-link-nexus-tools.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Symlink farm under test; the link is the subject, never executed; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-notify-gate.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	Invokes $WORK/fakebin/claude by ABSOLUTE path; no resolution occurs; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-pane-state.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	Stub is backgrounded by absolute path purely so the pane's comm reads claude; reach=0. (The issue guessed this one correctly.)
monitor/watcher/test-respawn-loop-integration.sh	path	no-claude-bin	guarded	exposed	The site #746 reported and #759 fixed. Measured: resolved to the decoy locals copy, not its own stub, and the guard refused.
monitor/watcher/test-respawn.sh	local	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $FAKE_NEXUS/node_modules/.bin/claude; measured reach=34, every one resolving there via step 2.
monitor/watcher/test-secondary-clone-state.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Three fixture roots, each with its own node_modules stub; measured reach=6, each resolving to the matching root.
monitor/watcher/test-spawn-fresh-orchestrator.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $FAKE_NEXUS/node_modules/.bin/claude; measured reach=30, all step 2.
monitor/watcher/test-spawn-worker-cwd.sh	path	claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Deliberately omits the node_modules stub and passes CLAUDE_BIN per invocation; measured reach=4, all resolving to $STUB_BIN/claude via step 1.
monitor/watcher/test-spawn-worker-reply-to.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $FAKE_NEXUS/node_modules/.bin/claude; measured reach=8, all step 2.
monitor/watcher/test-spawn-worker-resume.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $FAKE_NEXUS/node_modules/.bin/claude; measured reach=34, all step 2.
monitor/watcher/test-spawn-worker.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $FAKE_NEXUS/node_modules/.bin/claude; measured reach=25, all step 2.
monitor/watcher/test-stub-claude-manifest.sh	local	no-claude-bin	guarded	selftest	This suite. Its stub-creating lines are planted CONTROL fixtures for the classifier plus a synthetic #746 hazard; it drives both the refuse and the accept arm of th_require_stub_claude on purpose.
monitor/watcher/test-supervisor-liveness.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Empty node_modules/.bin/claude as a spawn precondition; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-trash-install.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	npm layout under test by the trash/install path; the symlink is the subject; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-watcher-singleton-groups.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at node_modules/.bin/claude as a spawn precondition; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-watcher-supervise.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Empty node_modules/.bin/claude as a spawn precondition; step 2; reach=0.
monitor/watcher/test-worker-nproc-bound.sh	local	no-claude-bin	unguarded	pinned	Stub at $FAKE_NEXUS/node_modules/.bin/claude, and its header already documents the step order; measured reach=3, all step 2.
monitor/watcher/test-pane-state-boot-absent.sh	path	no-claude-bin	unguarded	no-resolver	#788: copies a real binary to $CLAUDEBIN/claude so /proc/<pid>/comm reads `claude` (#554) and _pane_has_live_claude matches. MEASURED reach=0 with _claude-bin.sh instrumented across a full suite run: $CLAUDEBIN is a mktemp dir never added to PATH, both uses are ABSOLUTE paths inside a `tmux new-window` command string, and the file names neither CLAUDE_BIN nor _claude-bin.sh. The resolver is never sourced, so the #746 PATH re-fronting hazard cannot bite.
